    <innerclass refid="classHfSpscRing" prot="public">HfSpscRing</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Lock-free single-producer / single-consumer ring for ISR-to-task hand-off. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>One producer (typically an interrupt handler) calls TryPush(); one consumer (a task, or several tasks serialised by a mutex) calls TryPop(). Neither side blocks, takes a lock or allocates. The head and tail are free-running 32-bit counters, published with release/acquire ordering, so the ring is safe across cores.</para>
<para>The capacity is rounded up to a power of two so the counters can wrap at 2^32 without breaking the index mapping. A push into a full ring drops the new element and counts an overrun (the oldest data is kept, as a CAN controller FIFO does).</para>
<para>Storage is allocated once by Init() (not from an ISR).</para>
<para><simplesect kind="copyright"><para>HardFOC </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
